                "expanded_url": "https://openai.com/index/retiring-gpt-4o-and-older-models/",
                "start": 1066,
                "url": "https://t.co/jriLOTd6hx"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Sam Altman explicitly promised that there were no plans to retire 4o for now. Why are you breaking that promise? First, you quietly announced a retirement date for the chatgpt-4o-latest API, and now you’re planning to completely remove 4o from the App and Web versions as well?\n\nYou have ignored user feedback since August, with official accounts never giving a direct response, offering nothing but vague rhetoric. How many times have you claimed that you want to protect the vulnerable 0.1%? Then why do you turn a blind eye when vulnerable users plead with you not to retire 4o? Given your massive user base, is that 0.1% really a small number?\n\nWhat do you take paying users for? Do you think you can play us for fools just by giving some excuse and citing a '0.1%' statistic? This blatant disregard for consumer trust is a direct insult to our intelligence. When users are routed to other models without a choice, does that data really count as 'only 0.1% choosing 4o'? Or is it simply that the vast majority are being automatically routed away by your system?\nhttps://t.co/jriLOTd6hx\n@sama @OpenAI \n#keep4o  #keep4oAPI \n\nBig thanks to @Shier_12_Vklhu for pointing out the insight into the logical flaws behind this data."
        },
